    "created_at": "2016-06-07T21:21:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-07T21:21:40Z",
    "body": "I'm objecting to the spec change on the basis that I don't think this will be Web compatible.  Furthermore, all major UAs currently have this synchronous script execution behavior, and they are interoperable in this regard.\n\nGiven the purpose of standards is to allow new UA to be implemented by following it, I think it's actively hostile for someone trying to implement new engine (e.g. Servo) to have this change in the spec until some popular UA successfully ships with the asynchronous script execution behavior.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "reactions": {
